<title>GERMANY: Germany's OeTV chief to demand real wage gains.</title>
<headline>Germany's OeTV chief to demand real wage gains.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The leader of Germany's OeTV public-workers union said on Tuesday he would demand a real wage increase in upcoming contract negotiations for next year.</p>
<p>Herbert Mai told the Bild newspaper in an interview that a wage reduction or no real wage gain, which has been the case since 1993, would not be accepted because employers have not fulfilled their promise to create new jobs.</p>
<p>Instead of new job growth, Mai said there has been further job cuts in the public sector.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
